= Lugforth =

An unofficial fork of [uEforth https://github.com/flagxor/ueforth] (Bradley D. Nelson), a
Forth bootstrapped from a small C kernel, which I extended: SDL2 bindings (window,
drawing, sound, ABC music and soundfont), a graphical console with a color picker and
system fonts, a line editor with history and completion, two text editors (``ed`` for code,
``writhdeck`` for writing, with color themes including colorForth), examples (drum machine,
breakout, roguelike, piano roll), and ports: Android (one APK), web, Game Boy Advance,
Raspberry Pi Pico and ESP32. A single executable is enough on Linux (``lugforth``, or
``lugforth-mini`` without editors or SDL2), plus an AppImage and an APK.

[images/lugforth.png]

[github.com/luginf/lugforth https://github.com/luginf/lugforth] -
[website https://luginf.github.io/lugforth/] -
[downloads https://github.com/luginf/lugforth/releases]


= wmdcalc and wmdockapps =

wmdcalc is a small calculator dock app for [Window Maker https://www.windowmaker.org/],
with three input modes: Forth (reverse Polish notation), Lisp (s-expressions)
and classic. A popup window gives a larger keypad, and keyboard input and the
clipboard are supported. It is built on my fork of wmdockapps, a C++ library
for writing themed dock apps (the picture shows the apps shipped with it).

[images/wmdockapps.webp]

[github.com/luginf/wmdcalc https://github.com/luginf/wmdcalc] -
[github.com/luginf/wmdockapps https://github.com/luginf/wmdockapps]
